{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","id":"62a91e91630d940c253d7694","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260814222458.584906-1-weilin.chang%40arm.com/","channels":["linux-arm-kernel"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:20260814222458.584906-1-weilin.chang@arm.com","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260814222458.584906-1-weilin.chang%40arm.com/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:20260814222458.584906-1-weilin.chang@arm.com"},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v3 1/2] arm64: ptdump: Make note_page_flush() range aware","messages":{"nuba4no4mrqwswozt6sesavtzqupg3z5z5icjs5a22etbwnb35@cdqbdvbg2w4a":{"id":"nuba4no4mrqwswozt6sesavtzqupg3z5z5icjs5a22etbwnb35@cdqbdvbg2w4a","messageId":"nuba4no4mrqwswozt6sesavtzqupg3z5z5icjs5a22etbwnb35@cdqbdvbg2w4a","references":["20260814222458.584906-1-weilin.chang@arm.com","20260814222458.584906-2-weilin.chang@arm.com","86v79bzkq0.wl-maz@kernel.org"],"missingAncestorIds":["86v79bzkq0.wl-maz@kernel.org","20260814222458.584906-2-weilin.chang@arm.com","20260814222458.584906-1-weilin.chang@arm.com"],"author":{"name":"Wei-Lin Chang","address":"weilin.chang@arm.com"},"sender":{"name":"linux-arm-kernel","address":"linux-arm-kernel-bounces@lists.infradead.org"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Marc Zyngier","address":"maz@kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"kvmarm@lists.linux.dev"},{"name":"Catalin Marinas","address":"catalin.marinas@arm.com"},{"name":"Will Deacon","address":"will@kernel.org"},{"name":"Oliver Upton","address":"oupton@kernel.org"},{"name":"Fuad Tabba","address":"tabba@google.com"},{"name":"Joey Gouly","address":"joey.gouly@arm.com"},{"name":"Steffen Eiden","address":"seiden@linux.ibm.com"},{"name":"Suzuki K Poulose","address":"suzuki.poulose@arm.com"},{"name":"Zenghui Yu","address":"yuzenghui@huawei.com"},{"name":"Mike Rapoport (Microsoft)","address":"rppt@kernel.org"},{"name":"Ryan Roberts","address":"ryan.roberts@arm.com"},{"name":"David Hildenbrand (Arm)","address":"david@kernel.org"},{"name":"Anshuman Khandual","address":"anshuman.khandual@arm.com"},{"name":"Dev Jain","address":"dev.jain@arm.com"},{"name":"Ard Biesheuvel","address":"ardb@kernel.org"},{"name":"Mark Rutland","address":"mark.rutland@arm.com"},{"name":"Matt Fleming","address":"matt@codeblueprint.co.uk"},{"name":"Vincent Donnefort","address":"vdonnefort@google.com"},{"name":"Sebastian Ene","address":"sebastianene@google.com"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-15T23:16:54.000Z","iso":"2026-08-15T23:16:54.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v3 1/2] arm64: ptdump: Make note_page_flush() range aware","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-arm-kernel.lists.infradead.org","displayName":"linux-arm-kernel.lists.infradead.org","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On Sat, Aug 15, 2026 at 12:28:23PM +0100, Marc Zyngier wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"On Fri, 14 Aug 2026 23:24:57 +0100,"},{"depth":1,"text":"Wei-Lin Chang <weilin.chang@arm.com> wrote:"},{"depth":1,"text":"> "},{"depth":1,"text":"> note_page_flush() calls note_page() with addr == 0 and level == -1 to"},{"depth":1,"text":"> dump the last row of a ptdump. addr == 0 (1 << 64 wrapped around)"},{"depth":1,"text":"> renders a huge region with enormous size for address spaces with"},{"depth":1,"text":"> IA bits < 64. For example the stage-2 page tables and the EFI runtime"},{"depth":1,"text":"> page table."},{"depth":1,"text":"> "},{"depth":1,"text":"> More importantly, the last region of the address space and everything"},{"depth":1,"text":"> after the address space up to 1 << 64 are merged into one row of"},{"depth":1,"text":"> output. If the last region within the address space is valid, it will"},{"depth":1,"text":"> appear to remain valid up to 1 << 64 with the same attributes."},{"depth":1,"text":"> "},{"depth":1,"text":"> Currently only the EFI runtime ptdump is affected by this, but KVM will"},{"depth":1,"text":"> soon fix its stage-2 ptdump by using note_page_flush(). Here is an"},{"depth":1,"text":"> example of an EFI runtime ptdump (last row):"},{"depth":1,"text":"> "},{"depth":1,"text":"> 0x0000008000000000-0x0000000000000000   17179868672G PGD"},{"depth":1,"text":"> "},{"depth":1,"text":"> With this patch:"},{"depth":1,"text":"> "},{"depth":1,"text":"> 0x0000008000000000-0x0001000000000000      261632G PGD"},{"depth":1,"text":"> "},{"depth":1,"text":"> To fix this, cache the end address of a ptdump in ptdump_pg_state so"},{"depth":1,"text":"> note_page_flush() can call the final note_page() with the correct end"},{"depth":1,"text":"> address."},{"depth":1,"text":"> "},{"depth":1,"text":"> Fixes: 9d80448ac92b (\"efi/arm64: Add debugfs node to dump UEFI runtime page tables\")"},{"depth":1,"text":"> Signed-off-by: Wei-Lin Chang <weilin.chang@arm.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"> ---"},{"depth":1,"text":">  arch/arm64/include/asm/ptdump.h |  2 ++"},{"depth":1,"text":">  arch/arm64/mm/ptdump.c          | 14 +++++++++++++-"},{"depth":1,"text":">  2 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)"},{"depth":1,"text":"> "},{"depth":1,"text":"> diff --git a/arch/arm64/include/asm/ptdump.h b/arch/arm64/include/asm/ptdump.h"},{"depth":1,"text":"> index 5b374a6ab34a..1b743de7d89e 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"> --- a/arch/arm64/include/asm/ptdump.h"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +++ b/arch/arm64/include/asm/ptdump.h"},{"depth":1,"text":"> @@ -52,6 +52,8 @@ struct ptdump_pg_state {"},{"depth":1,"text":">  \tconst struct addr_marker *marker;"},{"depth":1,"text":">  \tconst struct mm_struct *mm;"},{"depth":1,"text":">  \tunsigned long start_address;"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t/* exclusive end, ULONG_MAX represents an end at 1 << 64 */"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\tunsigned long end_address;"},{"depth":1,"text":">  \tint level;"},{"depth":1,"text":">  \tptval_t current_prot;"},{"depth":1,"text":">  \tbool check_wx;"},{"depth":1,"text":"> diff --git a/arch/arm64/mm/ptdump.c b/arch/arm64/mm/ptdump.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"> index 1c20144700d7..eab400e744d9 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"> --- a/arch/arm64/mm/ptdump.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +++ b/arch/arm64/mm/ptdump.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"> @@ -278,9 +278,19 @@ void note_page_pgd(struct ptdump_state *pt_st, unsigned long addr, pgd_t pgd)"},{"depth":1,"text":">  "},{"depth":1,"text":">  void note_page_flush(struct ptdump_state *pt_st)"},{"depth":1,"text":">  {"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\tstruct ptdump_pg_state *st = container_of(pt_st, struct ptdump_pg_state, ptdump);"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\tunsigned long end = st->end_address;"},{"depth":1,"text":">  \tpte_t pte_zero = {0};"},{"depth":1,"text":">  "},{"depth":1,"text":"> -\tnote_page(pt_st, 0, -1, pte_val(pte_zero));"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t/*"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t * Address spaces that end at 1 << 64 have end_address == ULONG_MAX,"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t * but note_page() expects the exclusive end. In this case adjust end"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t * to the wraparound value 0."},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t */"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\tif (end == ULONG_MAX)"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\tend = 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\tnote_page(pt_st, end, -1, pte_val(pte_zero));"},{"depth":1,"text":">  }"},{"depth":1,"text":">  "},{"depth":1,"text":">  static void arm64_ptdump_walk_pgd(struct ptdump_state *st, struct mm_struct *mm)"},{"depth":1,"text":"> @@ -303,6 +313,7 @@ void ptdump_walk(struct seq_file *s, struct ptdump_info *info)"},{"depth":1,"text":">  \t\t.marker = info->markers,"},{"depth":1,"text":">  \t\t.mm = info->mm,"},{"depth":1,"text":">  \t\t.pg_level = &kernel_pg_levels[0],"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\t.end_address = end,"},{"depth":1,"text":">  \t\t.level = -1,"},{"depth":1,"text":">  \t\t.ptdump = {"},{"depth":1,"text":">  \t\t\t.note_page_pte = note_page_pte,"},{"depth":1,"text":"> @@ -344,6 +355,7 @@ bool ptdump_check_wx(void)"},{"depth":1,"text":">  \t\t\t{ -1, NULL},"},{"depth":1,"text":">  \t\t},"},{"depth":1,"text":">  \t\t.pg_level = &kernel_pg_levels[0],"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\t.end_address = ~0UL,"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"nit: shouldn't this be ULONG_MAX instead? Yes, this is the same thing,"},{"depth":1,"text":"but it doesn't hurt to match the documentation."}],"lineCount":89,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"I wrote ~0UL because the range[] initialization was using ~0UL so I did\nthe same for consistency. I think changing them both to ULONG_MAX is the\nbetter approach. I'll do that if a v4 is required."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Thanks,\nWei-Lin Chang"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Thanks,"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"\tM."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"-- "},{"depth":1,"text":"Without deviation from the norm, progress is not possible."}],"lineCount":7,"maximumDepth":1}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"86v79bzkq0.wl-maz@kernel.org"}},"rootIds":["nuba4no4mrqwswozt6sesavtzqupg3z5z5icjs5a22etbwnb35@cdqbdvbg2w4a"],"childrenByParent":{},"chronologicalIds":["nuba4no4mrqwswozt6sesavtzqupg3z5z5icjs5a22etbwnb35@cdqbdvbg2w4a"],"patchSeries":[],"diagnostics":[],"patches":{}}}